gradedModule(List) -- make a graded module
******************************************

  * Function: *note gradedModule: (Macaulay2Doc)gradedModule,
  * Usage: 
        gradedModule v
  * Inputs:
      * v, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a module, or a list or sequence
        of modules
  * Outputs:
      * a *note graded module: GradedModule,, the graded module with the i-th
        element of v installed as its i-th component

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : gradedModule ZZ^2             |
|                                   |
|           2                       |
|o1 = 0 : ZZ                        |
|                                   |
|o1 : GradedModule                  |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : gradedModule(ZZ^2,ZZ^3,ZZ^400)|
|                                   |
|           2                       |
|o2 = 0 : ZZ                        |
|                                   |
|           3                       |
|     1 : ZZ                        |
|                                   |
|           400                     |
|     2 : ZZ                        |
|                                   |
|o2 : GradedModule                  |
+-----------------------------------+
If v is a *note chain complex: ChainComplex, then the return value is the
graded module underlying it.
+---------------------------+
|i3 : R = QQ[x,y]           |
|                           |
|o3 = R                     |
|                           |
|o3 : PolynomialRing        |
+---------------------------+
|i4 : C = res coker vars R  |
|                           |
|      1      2      1      |
|o4 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0|
|                           |
|     0      1      2      3|
|                           |
|o4 : ChainComplex          |
+---------------------------+
|i5 : gradedModule C        |
|                           |
|          1                |
|o5 = 0 : R                 |
|                           |
|          2                |
|     1 : R                 |
|                           |
|          1                |
|     2 : R                 |
|                           |
|     3 : 0                 |
|                           |
|o5 : GradedModule          |
+---------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "gradedModule(ChainComplex)"
  * *note gradedModule(List): gradedModule_lpList_rp, -- make a graded module
  * "gradedModule(Module)"
  * "gradedModule(Sequence)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

