Ring ^ BettiTally -- construct a chain complex with prescribed Betti table
**************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        R^t
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * t, a *note Betti tally: (Macaulay2Doc)BettiTally,, 
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note chain complex: ChainComplex,, whose Betti table matches t; 

Description
===========

Given a ring $R$, a chain complex with zero maps over $R$ that has a prescribed
Betti table can be constructed. Negative entries are ignored and rational
entries produce an error. Multigraded rings work only if the Betti tally
contains degrees of the correct degree length.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : t = new BettiTally from { (0,{0},0) => 1, (1,{1},1) => 2, (2,{3},3) =>  |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1 2                                                            |
|o2 = total: 1 2 7                                                            |
|         0: 1 2 .                                                            |
|         1: . . 3                                                            |
|         2: . . 4                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : BettiTally                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3, (2,{4},4) => 4 }                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = R^t                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|      1      2      7                                                        |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : betti C                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1 2                                                            |
|o4 = total: 1 2 7                                                            |
|         0: 1 2 .                                                            |
|         1: . . 3                                                            |
|         2: . . 4                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : BettiTally                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C.dd                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|          1         2                                                        |
|o5 = 0 : R  <----- R  : 1                                                    |
|               0                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|          2         7                                                        |
|     1 : R  <----- R  : 2                                                    |
|               0                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : ComplexMap                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Contributors
============

Hans-Christian von Bothmer implemented this feature.

See also
========

