dd -- differential in a chain complex
*************************************

Description
===========

dd -- a symbol used as a key in a chain complex, under which are stored the
differentials.


The differentials are stored as the members in a chain complex map of degree
-1.  The map C.dd_i is the one whose source is the module C_i, and it is
arranged to be zero if no map has been stored in that spot.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b];              |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : C = resolution cokernel vars R|
|                                   |
|      1      2      1              |
|o2 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0        |
|                                   |
|     0      1      2      3        |
|                                   |
|o2 : ChainComplex                  |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : C.dd                          |
|                                   |
|          1               2        |
|o3 = 0 : R  <----------- R  : 1    |
|               | a b |             |
|                                   |
|          2                  1     |
|     1 : R  <-------------- R  : 2 |
|               {1} | -b |          |
|               {1} | a  |          |
|                                   |
|          1                        |
