ChainComplex ^ ZZ -- access member, cohomological degree
********************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        C^n
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note chain complex: ChainComplex,
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, The (-n)-th component C_(-n) of
        C

Description
===========

Subscripts refer to homological degree, and superscripts refer to cohomological
degree. It is only a matter of notation: C_(-n) is always the same as C^n.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : C = res coker vars R          |
|                                   |
|      1      3      3      1       |
|o2 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0 |
|                                   |
|     0      1      2      3      4 |
|                                   |
|o2 : ChainComplex                  |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : C = dual C                    |
|                                   |
|             1      3      3      1|
|o3 = 0  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R |
|                                   |
|     -4     -3     -2     -1     0 |
|                                   |
|o3 : ChainComplex                  |
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : C^2                           |
|                                   |
|      3                            |
|o4 = R                             |
|                                   |
|o4 : R-module, free, degrees {3:-2}|
+-----------------------------------+
|i5 : C^2 == C_(-2)                 |
|                                   |
|o5 = true                          |
+-----------------------------------+

