sum(ChainComplexMap) -- direct sum of the components of a chain map
*******************************************************************

  * Function: *note sum: (Macaulay2Doc)sum,

Description
===========

sum C -- yields the sum of the modules in a chain complex map.


The degrees of the components are preserved.
+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..c];            |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : C = res coker vars R         |
|                                  |
|      1      3      3      1      |
|o2 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0|
|                                  |
|     0      1      2      3      4|
|                                  |
|o2 : ChainComplex                 |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : sum C.dd                     |
|                                  |
|o3 = {0} | 0 a b c 0  0  0  0  |  |
|     {1} | 0 0 0 0 -b -c 0  0  |  |
|     {1} | 0 0 0 0 a  0  -c 0  |  |
|     {1} | 0 0 0 0 0  a  b  0  |  |
|     {2} | 0 0 0 0 0  0  0  c  |  |
|     {2} | 0 0 0 0 0  0  0  -b |  |
|     {2} | 0 0 0 0 0  0  0  a  |  |
|     {3} | 0 0 0 0 0  0  0  0  |  |
|                                  |
|             8      8             |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R              |
+----------------------------------+
|i4 : betti oo                     |
|                                  |
|            0 1                   |
|o4 = total: 8 8                   |
|        -1: . 1                   |
|         0: 1 3                   |
|         1: 3 3                   |
|         2: 3 1                   |
|         3: 1 .                   |
|                                  |
|o4 : BettiTally                   |
+----------------------------------+

