ChainComplexMap ^ ZZ -- iterated composition
********************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        f^n
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note chain complex map: ChainComplexMap,, or a a *note graded
        module map: GradedModuleMap,
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note chain complex map: ChainComplexMap,, the composite f o f o ...
        o f (n times)

Description
===========

If f is a *note GradedModuleMap: GradedModuleMap,, then so is the result.


One use of this function is to determine if a chain complex is well-defined.
The chain complex will be well-defined if the square of the differential is
zero.
+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];               |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : C = res coker vars R         |
|                                  |
|      1      3      3      1      |
|o2 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- 0|
|                                  |
|     0      1      2      3      4|
|                                  |
|o2 : ChainComplex                 |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : C.dd^2 == 0                  |
|                                  |
|o3 = true                         |
+----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ChainComplex: ChainComplex, -- the class of all chain complexes

