map(ChainComplex,ChainComplex,Function) -- make a map of chain complexes
************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map,
  * Usage: 
        map(C,D,f) or map(C,D,f,Degree=>d)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note chain complex: ChainComplex,
      * D, a *note chain complex: ChainComplex,
      * f, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, a function such that f(i)
        is a matrix D_i --> C_(i+d)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null,
      * *note DegreeLift: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null,
      * *note DegreeMap: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note chain complex map: ChainComplexMap,, a map of chain complexes D
        --> C

Description
===========

If the degree d is not given, then d=0 is assumed.


The function f is called only for those indices that represent spots occupied
in both the source and target chain complexes.

Caveat
======

This function does not check that the maps f(i) commute with the differential
of the chain complexes.

